# NOEZEMA evaluation corpus v2 (EVAL-3, §22.2)
# 50 seeded questions. Format: one JSON object per line: {"text": ..., "priority": N}.
# '#' lines are skipped by hostctl eval-run; lines are deduped by exact text.
#
# Structure (FIFO order = priority DESC, then created_at ASC, then id):
#   priority 100 — 3 temporal questions with OLD as_of (2026-04-15 / 2026-01-01):
#     committed first; after the mid-run v2->v3 activation their reverify_after
#     (as_of + 30d) is in the past, so the reassessment worker marks them DUE
#     (the due/stale + reassessment mechanism under test).
#   priority 90  — 11 pack anchors (7 URL-backed + 4 workspace-file):
#     each establishes one claim; the pack follow-ups (priority 80) run only
#     after every anchor is committed, so each follow-up session can see the
#     anchor claim in the knowledge context and reference it (significant_claim_reuse).
#   priority 80  — 22 pack follow-ups: re-verify the anchor fact from the same
#     two sources / the same file (exact-dedup or dependency edge => the anchor
#     claim is referenced by >=2 distinct sessions).
#   priority 0   — 14 standalone URL-backed questions (4 external_fact +
#     10 temporal_fact), random order among themselves (uuid tie-break).
#
# URL-backed questions (24 total: 11 anchors + 14 standalone - 1 overlap-free):
# every one names the fact to establish and exactly two sources on two
# different registrable domains (independence groups => E3 lift, the
# external_temporal_e3 gate). All 24 URL pairs were fact-verified within the
# 40 KB normalized-text budget before the freeze.
#
# Claim-type mix: 20 temporal_fact (17 current as_of + 3 old as_of) +
# 4 external_fact (stable facts) + local_observation (12 workspace questions)
# => due_stale denominator = 20 temporal claims (zero tolerance: every
# temporal question must yield a current-head temporal claim).

